# Axiom (product tasks + docs)

This product is bound to an Axiom workspace. **Tasks and settled product documentation live there**, not as ad-hoc TODOs in chat or duplicate markdown in the repo. If another product's ticket rule is also loaded in a multi-root workspace, ignore it — this repo writes only here.

**Language**: everything written to this workspace (ticket titles, bodies, comments, docs) is English. Keep code identifiers, paths, and tool names as they are in the repo.

## Binding

Read `.axiom.json` at the repo root before any Axiom MCP call:

- `tenant_slug` / `workspace_slug` — product boundary (one workspace per product)
- `projects.audits` / `projects.features` / `projects.bugs` — the three ticket boards
- `docs.*` — UUIDs for settled docs (Overview, Architecture, Decisions)

If the file is missing or IDs are stale, follow the `axiom` skill to bootstrap or repair — do not invent workspace/project IDs.

## Ticket buckets (pick one project)

| Project      | Use for                                                                |
| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Features** | New capabilities, domains, enhancements, agreed delivery work          |
| **Bugs**     | Defects, regressions, incorrect behavior                               |
| **Audits**   | Convention/structure/security reviews, checklist-driven pass/fail work |

Work-in-progress and delivery status live **only on tickets** (`backlog` / `todo` / `doing` / `done`, comments). Do not keep a Progress/changelog doc. Axiom has no phases — do not send `phase_name`.

## Docs = settled knowledge

Docs are for things that should stay true after the work lands — not a running diary.

- **Overview** — what the product is, for whom
- **Architecture** — how it is structured (update when the structure actually changes)
- **Decisions** — ADRs for real choices that stick

## When to write to Axiom

- **Agreed, actionable work** → `create_task` on the matching bucket (`status`: `todo` when ready to pick up, `backlog` when not). Do not spam micro-todos.
- **Starting / finishing work** → `doing` while implementing; `done` only once the work is on `main`. Unpushed work stays `doing`. Comment outcomes on the ticket.
- **Design or product decision (settled)** → append a dated section to Decisions.
- **Domain / structure change (landed)** → update Architecture.

### Audits (required)

Every convention / structure / security audit goes on the **Audits** board (`projects.audits.slug`). Do not leave findings only in chat.

1. **Start** — `create_task` on Audits (`status`: `doing`) with scope, verdict placeholder, and checklist.
2. **While auditing** — put the full report in the task body: Summary, Critical / Warning / Note with paths, checks run (lint/typecheck), out of scope.
3. **While remediating** — note what was fixed vs deferred on the ticket (comment or append).
4. **Finish** — when the audit (and any agreed fixes) are done, `complete_task` or `update_task` → `done` (only if the work is on `main`). Link the task in the chat reply.

Follow `.cursor/skills/audit/SKILL.md` for the audit workflow; this rule is the documentation invariant.

Code conventions stay in `.cursor/rules` and the repo. Product knowledge stays in Axiom.

## MCP usage

Use the Axiom MCP (`user-axiom`). Always pass `workspace_slug` from the binding. Prefer `project_slug` / doc UUIDs from `.axiom.json`. Discover tool schemas with MCP tool listing before calling.

| Where             | Link                                                                                                         |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Cursor chat**   | `https://axiom.fecruzb.com/app/<tenant_slug>/w/<workspace_slug>/p/<project>/t/<taskId>` (docs: `/d/<docId>`) |
| **Axiom content** | `[Title](axiom:doc/<workspace_slug>/<docId>)` / `[Title](axiom:task/<workspace_slug>/<project>/<taskId>)`    |

Day-to-day workflows and bootstrap: `.cursor/skills/axiom/SKILL.md`.
